---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Missed-Call Calculator
description: What are missed calls really costing your business? Use your own numbers — customer value, missed calls, booking rate — and see the revenue walking out the door.
pageCss: roi
permalink: /roi/
# ── GHL form id for "Free Website Scorecard - ROI Calculator": a duplicate of the
#    /scorecard/ form (J9WkThXTnIN59SBHNPxX). Attribution comes from the form
#    IDENTITY, not a hidden field — submissions are tracked per form, so a lead
#    arriving here is distinguishable from one on /scorecard/ or /score/ with no
#    extra field to maintain.
#    Same three fields (Full Name / Website / Email), same fulfilment, no phone
#    field — so this capture carries no A2P surface.
#    Verified 2026-08-08 against the public widget config: actionType 2
#    (thank-you message), redirectUrl empty — it did NOT inherit a redirect.
#    Deliberately inline rather than in _data/site.json, matching start.njk.
scorecardRoiFormId: "FFjmbww4O3Uf48asjxaf"
---
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import icon %}

<div class="header-band">
  <span class="header-eyebrow">The Math</span>
  <h1>What are missed calls <em>really</em> costing you?</h1>
  <p>No made-up industry stats. Drag three sliders with your own numbers and see what walks out the door when nobody answers.</p>
</div>

<div class="wrap">
  <div class="calc-card fade-in">
    <div class="sliders">
      <div class="slider-row">
        <div class="slider-head">
          <label for="rTicket">What's a new customer worth to you?</label>
          <span class="slider-val" id="rTicketV">$300</span>
        </div>
        <input type="range" id="rTicket" min="25" max="3000" step="25" value="300" aria-describedby="rTicketHint">
        <p class="slider-hint" id="rTicketHint">Think beyond the first visit — a good customer usually comes back.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="slider-row">
        <div class="slider-head">
          <label for="rLeads">Calls &amp; messages you miss in a month</label>
          <span class="slider-val" id="rLeadsV">10</span>
        </div>
        <input type="range" id="rLeads" min="1" max="50" step="1" value="10" aria-describedby="rLeadsHint">
        <p class="slider-hint" id="rLeadsHint">Busy with a customer, after hours, on the other line — the ones that go to voicemail or nowhere.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="slider-row">
        <div class="slider-head">
          <label for="rClose">How many would book if answered instantly?</label>
          <span class="slider-val" id="rCloseV">30%</span>
        </div>
        <input type="range" id="rClose" min="10" max="70" step="5" value="30" aria-describedby="rCloseHint">
        <p class="slider-hint" id="rCloseHint">Your normal booking rate, applied to the people you never got to answer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="result" role="status" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="result-label">Walking out the door</div>
      <div class="result-big"><span id="rMonthly">$900</span><span class="result-suffix">/month</span></div>
      <div class="result-year">That's <strong id="rYearly">$10,800</strong> a year — from customers who already tried to reach you.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="honesty fade-in">Your sliders, your math: missed calls × your booking rate × what a customer is worth.
    We don't pad it with "industry averages" — the honest number is convincing enough.</p>
</div>

<!-- ── CAPTURE ── the number above is the highest-intent moment on the site.
     Before this block it had no next step but the nav. Offer is the same free
     12-point scorecard /scorecard/ fulfils; the form is a duplicate carrying a
     hidden source value so calculator leads are attributable. -->
<section class="capture" id="breakdown">
  <div class="capture-inner fade-in">
    <div class="capture-content">
      <div class="section-label">The Other Half</div>
      <h2 class="capture-title">That's the <em>what.</em> Here's the <em>why.</em></h2>
      <p class="capture-sub">The number above tells you what's walking out the door. It can't tell you
        <strong>why</strong> those callers went looking somewhere else in the first place — that part is
        usually sitting on your website. We'll grade yours by hand, twelve checks, and send it back with
        the receipts.</p>
      <div class="capture-bullets">
        <div class="cap-bullet"><div class="cap-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon("check") }}</div><div class="cap-text"><strong>Free, and free of strings</strong><span>No card, no call required, no automated upsell.</span></div></div>
        <div class="cap-bullet"><div class="cap-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon("clock") }}</div><div class="cap-text"><strong>Back within 24 hours</strong><span>Graded by a person here in the Flathead, not a plugin.</span></div></div>
        <div class="cap-bullet"><div class="cap-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon("lock") }}</div><div class="cap-text"><strong>Your numbers stay on this page</strong><span>The sliders are yours. We don't need them to grade your site.</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capture-form">
      <div class="capture-form-title">Send me the scorecard</div>
      <p class="capture-form-sub">Name, website, email. Nothing else.</p>

      {% if scorecardRoiFormId %}
      <!-- Never add loading="lazy" — form_embed.js can't hook it and the iframe
           collapses to zero height. -->
      <iframe
        src="https://api.leadconnectorhq.com/widget/form/{{ scorecardRoiFormId }}"
        style="width:100%;min-height:460px;border:none;border-radius:8px"
        id="inline-{{ scorecardRoiFormId }}"
        data-layout="{'id':'INLINE'}"
        data-trigger-type="alwaysShow"
        data-activation-type="alwaysActivated"
        data-deactivation-type="neverDeactivate"
        data-form-name="Free Website Scorecard — ROI"
        data-height="460"
        data-layout-iframe-id="inline-{{ scorecardRoiFormId }}"
        data-form-id="{{ scorecardRoiFormId }}"
        title="Free website scorecard request form"
      ></iframe>
      <script src="https://link.msgsndr.com/js/form_embed.js"></script>
      {% else %}
      {# FALLBACK — public-safe by design. Until scorecardRoiFormId is set this
         must read as a normal CTA, never as developer instructions: it renders
         to real visitors on a live page. Hands off to /scorecard/, which carries
         the same form. #}
      <div class="form-fallback">
        <p>Takes about thirty seconds, and the scorecard comes back within a day.</p>
        <a href="/scorecard/" class="btn-primary">Get my free scorecard</a>
        <span class="form-fallback-note">Free, no card, no obligation.</span>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="context">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="section-head fade-in">
      <div class="section-label">Why It Adds Up</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">You never hear the calls you miss.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">A missed call doesn't complain — it just books somewhere else. The customers you lose
        this way never show up in any report, which is why the leak feels invisible until you do the math above.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ctx-grid fade-in">
      <div class="ctx-cell"><h3>While you're working</h3><p>Mid-haircut, mid-appointment, mid-job — exactly when you can't pick up is when the next customer calls.</p></div>
      <div class="ctx-cell"><h3>After hours</h3><p>People search and reach out at night and on Sundays. If nothing answers, the next result on Google does.</p></div>
      <div class="ctx-cell"><h3>Voicemail isn't a safety net</h3><p>Callers who wanted an answer now rarely wait for a callback — they just dial the next place on the list.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="section-inner fade-in">
    <h2>Now watch it get caught.</h2>
    <p>406 Front Desk answers every call and text — instantly, 24/7 — books the appointment, and follows up.
      Recovering even a customer or two a month usually covers it. <a href="/pricing/">See pricing</a>,
      <a href="/demo/">try the live demo</a>, or bring the numbers you just worked out to a twenty-minute call:</p>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <a href="/start/" class="btn-primary">Start here</a>
      <a href="tel:+14068400404" class="btn-secondary">Call (406) 840-0404</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  (function () {
    var t = document.getElementById("rTicket"),
        l = document.getElementById("rLeads"),
        c = document.getElementById("rClose");
    function fmt(n) { return "$" + Math.round(n).toLocaleString(); }
    function render() {
      document.getElementById("rTicketV").textContent = fmt(t.value);
      document.getElementById("rLeadsV").textContent = l.value;
      document.getElementById("rCloseV").textContent = c.value + "%";
      var monthly = l.value * (c.value / 100) * t.value;
      document.getElementById("rMonthly").textContent = fmt(monthly);
      document.getElementById("rYearly").textContent = fmt(monthly * 12);
    }
    [t, l, c].forEach(function (s) { s.addEventListener("input", render); });
    render();
  })();

  var observer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
    entries.forEach(function (e) { if (e.isIntersecting) e.target.classList.add("visible"); });
  }, { threshold: 0.1 });
  document.querySelectorAll(".fade-in").forEach(function (el) { observer.observe(el); });
</script>
